# ============================================================================
# Mountie: everything you might want to open as a drive, in one place.
#
#   SSH        a folder on a server: a drive letter on Windows (WinFsp, or
#              Windows' own WebDAV client), a folder in Files on Linux and
#              macOS (sshfs), the Files app on Android. Password, key or the
#              SSH agent; the server's key remembered; Act as root or
#              www-data through sudo.
#   ISO        disk images: ISO, IMG, DMG.
#   VHD        virtual disks: VHD, VHDX (and VMDK, QCOW2, VDI on Linux).
#   Partitions the computer's own disks and sticks, mounted and unmounted.
#
#   Lives in the tray, mounts what you ask by itself, can start with the
#   computer. Everything is kept on this device only.
# ============================================================================

@Window Mountie
Title=Mountie
Version=1.1
Width=480
Height=700
Icon=mountie.png
OnOpened=Start
OnClosing=Closing

